01,99,116,101,100,32,112,97,116,104,47,100,101,108,105,118,101,114,121,32,115,111,117,114,99,101,44,32,97,110,100,32,112,101,114,102,111,114,109,115,32,114,101,97,100,98,97,99,107,32,98,101,102,111,114,101,32,114,101,112,111,114,116,105,110,103,32,115,117,99,99,101,115,115,46,32,96,79,75,96,47,96,77,73,83,83,73,78,71,96,47,96,67,79,78,70,76,73,67,84,96,32,101,120,105,116,32,48,32,98,101,99,97,117,115,101,32,116,104,101,121,32,97,114,101,32,109,101,97,115,117,114,101,100,32,111,117,116,99,111,109,101,115,59,32,111,112,101,114,97,116,105,111,110,97,108,32,101,114,114,111,114,115,32,97,110,100,32,114,101,97,100,98,97,99,107,32,102,97,105,108,117,114,101,115,32,101,120,105,116,32,50,46,32,96,45,45,102,111,114,99,101,96,32,111,118,101,114,119,114,105,116,101,115,32,97,110,32,101,120,105,115,116,105,110,103,32,99,111,108,108,101,99,116,101,100,32,114,101,112,111,114,116,32,97,102,116,101,114,32,97,32,99,111,110,102,108,105,99,116,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],"stderr":[],"exit_code":0,"match_count":14,"file_matches":[{"path":"/Users/kimhawk/.local/state/h-mad/grok-audit-surface/run-ab2c85dc2e25-20261023T034641Z/roots/gas-root-d1-s1-efd_5thw/h-mad/SKILL.md","matches":[{"line_number":1719,"content":"   in `/tmp` until `collect-report --surface teammate` runs. Skipped once, the sheet cited three"},{"line_number":1721,"content":"   dispatching a single author — anything but `COLLECT: OK` is a halt, not a warning."},{"line_number":2847,"content":"6.6. **Report-file transport (preferred under Orca).** If `hmad-dispatch env` reports `substrate: orca`, replace `<REPORT_FILE_PATH>` with an absolute staged path `RP=/tmp/audit_<feature>_<phase>_cycle<N>_run$RUN.report.md`, minting `RUN=$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)-$$` once per dispatch and using it for the staged prompt too (step 7), so no dispatch ever reuses a report or prompt path. A hand assembly claims nothing: minting a fresh `RUN` is its only guard (only the script claims both paths and HALTs on reuse). Carry the literal `RUN` and `RP` values into steps 7–9, since each Bash call is a fresh shell; the agent will write its report there and mark `$RP.done`. Otherwise (cmux / unpinned) leave `<REPORT_FILE_PATH>` empty and rely on the sentinel scrape. Measured on `audit-cycle-verb`: across the 18 impl-plan audit passes, 17 delivered via the report file (file present, non-empty, `.done` written); 1 did not — cycle 7 pass 1 wrote neither the report file nor the marker, and its report w [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":3009,"content":"COLLECT_OUT=$(hmad-dispatch collect-report --surface codex \\"},{"line_number":3016,"content":"Read the `COLLECT:` token. Anything except `COLLECT: OK` is a delivery failure:"},{"line_number":3017,"content":"halt `<phase>:report_not_collected` and print `[H-MAD] <feature> <phase> halted reason=report_not_collected`."},{"line_number":3018,"content":"Only the path printed on the `COLLECT: OK` line is gateable; the transport file"},{"line_number":3022,"content":"if ! printf '%s\\n' \"$COLLECT_OUT\" | grep -q '^COLLECT: OK '; then"},{"line_number":3023,"content":"  printf '%s\\n' '[H-MAD] <feature> <phase> halted reason=report_not_collected'"},{"line_number":3025,"content":"  DOCS=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$COLLECT_OUT\" | sed -n 's/^COLLECT: OK path=\\(.*\\) delivered=.*/\\1/p')"},{"line_number":3101,"content":"COLLECT_OUT=$(hmad-dispatch collect-report --surface teammate \\"},{"line_number":3108,"content":"Read the `COLLECT:` token exactly as the codex leg does — anything but `COLLECT: OK` is"},{"line_number":3109,"content":"`<phase>:report_not_collected`, and only the path on the `COLLECT: OK` line is gateable."},{"line_number":3181,"content":"- `h_mad_collect_report.py` — collect-report surface collector: copies a delivered report-file or `--out` fallback into the docs audit path (the fallback reads a pane scrape past the dispatch boundary and an `exec` `--out` file from its end — see §6.6; conflating the two made it dead for `exec`), prints `COLLECT: OK|MISSING|CONFLICT` plus the collected path/delivery source, and performs readback before reporting success. `OK`/`MISSING`/`CONFLICT` exit 0 because they are measured outcomes; operational errors and readback failures exit 2. `--force` overwrites an existing collected report after a conflict."}]}]},"locations":[]}
{"type":"thought","data":"The feature is already"}
{"type":"thought","data":" implemented."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nAuditing the PLAN "}
{"type":"thought","data":"document for internal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contradictions, spec"}
{"type":"thought","data":" reconciliation issues,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" false platform claims,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and invariant breaches."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The pre-implementation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" tree descriptions may"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be stale now that the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" feature exists."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nGit history will help"}
{"type":"thought","data":" verify whether the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"plan's pre-change assumptions"}
{"type":"thought","data":" were wrong. The inlined"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plan text must be compared"}
{"type":"thought","data":" against the file on"}
{"type":"thought","data":" disk. The spec file"}
{"type":"thought","data":" also needs review. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Load-bearing claims "}
{"type":"thought","data":"will be checked with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" commands."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan's success"}
{"type":"thought","data":" criteria claims 25 "}
{"type":"thought","data":"mutations, but the spec"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and actual JSON contain"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exactly 23. This is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a real miscount in "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the plan. It is a must-fix"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contradiction because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the success bar is "}
{"type":"thought","data":"unsatisfiable against"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the enumerated contract."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe scope claims a"}
{"type":"thought","data":" `<feature>` slot, but"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the requirements specify"}
{"type":"thought","data":" \"stem\". The gate code"}
{"type":"thought","data":" prints `[H-MAD] {feature}"}
{"type":"thought","data":" gate INVALID`, so the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" derivation of `feature`"}
{"type":"thought","data":" must be checked against"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the plan text."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe audit targets "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the PLAN document itself,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" not the code. Internal"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contradictions in the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plan are findings regardless"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of whether the code"}
{"type":"thought","data":" matches.\n\nThe GATE_RE"}
{"type":"thought","data":" assumption may be wrong"}
{"type":"thought","data":" relative to current"}
{"type":"thought","data":" code. Git history will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" show when that regex"}
{"type":"thought","data":" was introduced."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe plan's regex assumption"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is factually wrong."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The current gate code"}
{"type":"thought","data":" uses a more permissive"}
{"type":"thought","data":" pattern that includes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a trailing-field group,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but the plan describes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a stricter version "}
{"type":"thought","data":"without it. This is "}
{"type":"thought","data":"a false premise. Whether"}
{"type":"thought","data":" it classifies as a "}
{"type":"thought","data":"build issue depends "}
{"type":"thought","data":"on whether an implementer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" would write a different"}
{"type":"thought","data":" parser based on this"}
{"type":"thought","data":" claim."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe false regex claim"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is a build issue. It"}
{"type":"thought","data":" misdescribes the platform"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and could mislead implementers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" about token compatibility."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The current output "}
{"type":"thought","data":"still matches both regexes,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" so this does not affect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the feature itself."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe regex claim is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a should-fix or measurement"}
{"type":"thought","data":" issue. The required"}
{"type":"thought","data":" output still matches"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the real regex, so "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the load-bearing conclusion"}
